# Shared (`packages/shared`)

This package is the source of truth for types and validation used by both `apps/api` and `apps/web`.

- Keep domain fields **snake_case** (`license_plate`, `fuel_level`, `active_alerts`, `connection_id`).
- Put Zod schemas and parse helpers here. Do not copy them into the API or the frontend.
- Validation messages stay German; exported `code`-style identifiers stay English. Alerts live in `parseAlertListQuery` / `parseAlertPatch` (`type`, `severity`, `resolved_at`, `ended_at`, `details`); `active_alerts` remains the unresolved count on the vehicle; `speeding_open` is the unfinished SPEEDING event. Drivers live in `parseDriverListQuery`. Live tempo bands live in `speedBand` (current `limit_kmh` + `speeding_open`). `formatAlertEvent` is the inbox event line.
- Export new public types/helpers from `src/index.ts`.
- List query, telemetry history limits, SSE focus (`STREAM_FOCUS_MAX_IDS`), fleet positions (`parseFleetPositionsQuery`, `FLEET_POSITIONS_MAX`, `FLEET_DRIVERS_MAX`), fleet driver search (`parseFleetDriversQuery`, `FLEET_DRIVERS_LIST_LIMIT` page size, `page`), sim pause (`parseSimPatch`), login (`parseLoginInput`), alerts (`parseAlertListQuery` including optional `type`, `parseAlertPatch`), drivers (`parseDriverListQuery`), and speed bands (`speedBand`) are part of this contract — changing them is an API change. Update API tests when the contract changes.
- The polyline codec (`src/geo/polyline.ts`) belongs here because both sides must agree on the encoding: the API appends with `encodePoint`, the map reads with `decodePolyline`. Precision 5 is part of the wire format — do not change it on one side.
